WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.690
The second season of DC Universe's Titans
has come to a close.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.920
While the finale episode, "Nightwing," doesn't
end on the cliffhanger the first season did,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.690
it also doesn't fail to raise more questions
than it answers.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.339
Kory's powers prove less reliable over the
season's last couple of episodes, and by "Nightwing"

00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:19.100
they disappear completely.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.961
She's shocked to learn she's lost any immunity
to bullets when Deathstroke shoots her early

00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:23.961
in the episode.

00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:27.929
She hasn't been able to use her energy weapons
since the previous episode, and her brief

00:00:27.929 --> 00:00:32.150
and embarrassingly futile attempt to put a
dent in Superboy with her fists proves that

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.950
her abilities have completely left her.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.520
So far, though, we have no idea what the cause
of her power loss is.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.800
Whatever has drained Kory's powers from her,
Blackfire certainly seems like the most likely

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.800
culprit.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.710
It isn't clear how Kory's sister could've
made it happen, but evil alien queens aren't

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.870
known for their lack of resources.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:52.450
The final scene of "Nightwing" - in which
we see Blackfire arrive on Earth - suggests

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.730
she has big plans for her sister.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.810
Another possibility is that her power loss
is psychosomatic, like the fluctuation of

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:10.250
Spider-Man's powers in 2004's Spider-Man 2.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.420
Since the beginning of Titans' second season,
Kory has learned her sister has stolen her

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.030
throne, her family has been killed, and finally
Kory is forced to kill a former lover.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.310
Honestly, she probably has way more stress
than Peter Parker ever did.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.189
As soon as it was confirmed at the end of
the eleventh episode that Jericho was alive,

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:30.950
we've wondered exactly how Dick Grayson planned
on saving his old friend.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.869
Killing Deathstroke would presumably kill
Jericho as well, unless he had another body

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:36.070
to jump into.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.020
Rose solves the problem in "Nightwing" by
offering her body up to Jericho to inhabit

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.250
before finally killing their sinister father.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.469
Now that we know how Jericho is saved, we're
left asking exactly how this brother/sister

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:48.619
pair is going to live with their shared body.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:52.700
From what little we see of Jericho's time
in his father's body, it seems clear Deathstroke

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.929
never willingly gave up control to his son,
whereas Rose lets her brother emerge right

00:01:56.929 --> 00:01:58.610
away so he can talk to Dick.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.780
This drastic shift for both characters isn't
going to be easy.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.369
For now, Jericho is likely grateful to have
any time in the world at all, but soon tensions

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:08.929
are bound to rise between him and Rose.

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:13.000
One moment in "Nightwing" that likely raised
a lot of questions for fans is the supposed

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.840
death of Slade Wilson, a.k.a. Deathstroke.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:21.630
Rose runs her father through with her sword,
and Dick confirms the assassin's death.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.750
"Is he...dead?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:26.750
Yeah."

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.750
Not so fast, Dick.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.810
In season 2's penultimate episode we see the
extent of Rose's healing powers.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.680
She puts the muzzle of a gun to her hand and
blows a hole through it, only to have the

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.430
flesh heal moments later.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:41.260
Rose inherited these healing powers from her
father, so you would think it would take more

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.819
than a sword to the chest to take him out
for good.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:47.450
Perhaps it's as simple as Slade's healing
powers not being quite as powerful as they

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.170
are in the comics, but we're just not convinced
that we've seen the last of him.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.140
Remember, this isn't the first time the Titans
thought he was dead.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.400
"I thought he was dead.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.600
Yeah, we all did.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.569
But he's alive and well in San Francisco."

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:05.390
Maybe the Titans version doesn't have a healing
factor as beefy as Wolverine's or Deadpool's,

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.130
but a sword through the chest still seems
far too easy of a way to die for a man who

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:14.060
single-handedly killed a handful of Themysciran
warriors before beating the tar out of Donna

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.409
Troy earlier in season 2.

00:03:16.409 --> 00:03:21.120
Some of the most tragic circumstances to befall
any of the Titans are forced upon Gar in season

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.120
2.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.840
For the past few episodes, Gar's been suffering
from a mental reconditioning courtesy of Mercy

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.489
Graves and Cadmus Laboratories.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:31.980
When the right piece of classical music is
played, Gar shifts into his tiger form and

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.379
kills anyone unlucky enough to be nearby.

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:38.500
In "Nightwing," Rachel is able to cut through
Cadmus' conditioning with her powers and bring

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.969
Gar back to sanity.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:45.269
But will it stick?

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:50.420
"Okay Gar that was not cool"

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.499
Gar's brainwashing wasn't the sort of demonic
possession that many of the other Titans had

00:03:54.499 --> 00:03:57.030
suffered at the hands of Trigon in the season
premiere.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.409
It could be that Rachel's powers healed the
damage that was done to Gar completely, but

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:05.709
it could also be that she was only able to
break him out of that particular violent episode.

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:09.780
It seems likely that no one will know for
sure if Gar is free and clear from Cadmus'

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.770
conditioning until the next time he hears
that same classical music.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:17.479
Unfortunately, if Gar does still prove susceptible
to the trigger, with Rachel in Themyscira

00:04:17.479 --> 00:04:22.670
the Titans may find themselves unable to stop
their friend from going on a rampage.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:27.250
In season 2's penultimate episode, Jason Todd
does not react well to the revelation that

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.919
Rose was originally meant to be Deathstroke's
mole among the Titans.

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:35.090
In spite of Rose assuring Jason her feelings
for him changed her loyalties, it's too much

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.340
for the already troubled young Robin to bear.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.500
He leaves Rose and is completely absent from
the two climactic fights in "Nightwing."

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.210
We don't see him until he appears on a motorcycle
when the Titans transfer Donna Troy's body

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:50.710
to the Themyscirans - presumably both as a
final show of respect to his former teammate,

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.990
as well as a way to let Dick know not to expect
to see him any time soon.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:55.990
But is he gone for good?

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:59.520
Jason Todd has a rocky history in the comics
and animated films.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.960
The second boy to wear Robin's costume eventually
dies at the hands of the Joker and returns

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:10.780
years later as the Red Hood.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.910
"Jason."

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.040
"Yes."

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.210
We have no way of knowing if Jason will go
down similar roads in Titans, but while Dick

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.139
and Bruce might show the minimum of respect
for his decisions, it seems unlikely they

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:27.800
won't at least keep tabs on him, if not outright
try to bring him back to the fold.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.610
Donna Troy's death after the battle with the
brainwashed Superboy in "Nightwing" came as

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:35.670
a surprise for everyone, although it's fair
to say that nobody was more shocked than Donna

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:42.639
herself.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:46.330
But what we've seen from Donna would suggest
she should be able to survive the injury that

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.340
kills her.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.300
Moments before, Donna proves to be the only
member of the Titans able to actually trade

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.349
blows with Conner.

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:56.450
Though she clearly doesn't win the fight,
a person surviving even a couple of unrestrained

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.449
blows from someone with the power of Superman
would suggest they don't die easy.

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:04.509
It could be that Donna's death is a set up
for the character's return sometime in season

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:06.050
3 or beyond.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.880
Rachel leaves for Themyscira specifically
with the goal of finding a way to bring Donna

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.570
back, and it wouldn't be the first time the
character was rescued from the land of the

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.570
dead.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:18.590
The Donna Troy of the comics was believed
killed in the 2003 miniseries Titans/Young

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.000
Justice: Graduation Day, only for that to
be a fake-out.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.879
She came back to the Titans in a 2005 series
whose title might very well end up being the

00:06:26.879 --> 00:06:31.250
name of a season 3 Titans episode - The Return
of Donna Troy.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:36.530
Throughout Titans' second season, we see Rachel's
powers manifest in lots of unpredictable ways.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:40.800
We see her unintentionally hurt both herself
and Gar in her sleep with it.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.860
Perhaps most shockingly, in "Fallen" Rachel's
abilities - without her knowledge or intent

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:49.139
- bring a stone gargoyle to life that hunts
down a new friend's abusive father.

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:53.880
By the end of "Nightwing," we learn the summons
that Rachel, Kory, Donna, and Dawn received

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:59.080
to meet Bruce Wayne at a diner in Nevada didn't
come from the real Bruce, and everything Kory

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:03.300
has seen leads her to believe Rachel somehow
unconsciously made it all happen.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.650
At the same time, the season 2 finale sees
Rachel's powers evolve to the point where

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.129
she can use them to heal.

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:13.020
She wakes Gar from his mental conditioning,
and with the touch of her hand heals Kory's

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.030
gunshot wound.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:18.169
She seems to think she may actually be able
to bring Donna Troy back from the dead, and

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:21.449
boards the plane to Themyscira in hopes of
doing just that.

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:23.550
So, what's going on with Rachel's powers?

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:27.870
All we know for sure is that Rachel's father
is defeated long before she has a chance to

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.530
learn the true limits of her abilities.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:33.240
Themyscira might be the perfect place for
Rachel to learn more.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.440
In the flashback episode "Aqualad," the OG
Titan Aqualad dies at Deathstroke's hands.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.240
In "Jericho," we learn that Aqualad wasn't
Slade Wilson's real target.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.699
It's revealed that Jillian - the older Themysciran
museum curator who seems to be part benefactor

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:51.180
and part mentor to Donna Troy - was Slade's
quarry.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:55.711
Before his fateful battle with Dick Grayson
that ends with Jericho's presumed death, Deathstroke

00:07:55.711 --> 00:07:58.199
makes good on his contract and gets rid of
Jillian.

00:07:58.199 --> 00:08:01.729
What we never learn is exactly why Jillian's
head was on the chopping block.

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:06.560
It isn't difficult to imagine that a Themysciran
like Jillian has made enemies over the years,

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.169
but we don't get any specifics.

00:08:08.169 --> 00:08:12.379
What's even more curious is that when Wintergreen
first gives Slade the details of the contract

00:08:12.379 --> 00:08:14.879
in "Aqualad," he describes it as "easy."

00:08:14.879 --> 00:08:20.750
The idea of targeting any Themysciran and
describing the job as "easy" is insane.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.789
Lex Luthor has yet to make an appearance in
Titans beyond pictures of him as a child,

00:08:24.789 --> 00:08:29.090
but Superman's arch-nemesis still has a powerful
presence in the show's second season.

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:34.029
In the episode "Conner," Superboy learns his
DNA is a combination of Luthor's and Superman's.

00:08:34.029 --> 00:08:38.289
The young hero visits Luthor's elderly father
in Smallville, and it doesn't take long before

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:41.459
we learn Luthor is behind the experiments
that created Conner.

00:08:41.459 --> 00:08:45.750
Toward the end of "Nightwing," Mercy Graves
is more than a little concerned to learn Luthor

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:50.850
is on the phone waiting to hear about her
failure.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.829
"It's Mr. Luthor."

00:08:55.829 --> 00:09:01.100
It seems like Lex Luthor has been groomed
to be for season 3 what Bruce Wayne was to

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.100
season 2.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.420
While there's been no confirmation as of yet
that Luthor will appear in Titans' third go-around,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:10.320
it doesn't seem likely that the billionaire
would allow his creation, Superboy, to remain

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.840
in the company of his greatest enemy's allies.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:17.390
Obviously, Titans is about the Titans and
the integrity of the show would suffer if

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.310
suddenly Aquaman and the Flash started regularly
showing up on the series.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:25.779
Still, considering the events of season 2,
the question has to be asked - exactly where

00:09:25.779 --> 00:09:28.850
is the Justice League and why aren't they
getting more involved?

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:31.230
"OH, NO."

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:34.949
By the end of "Nightwing," the history of
the Titans has seen the deaths of two sidekicks

00:09:34.949 --> 00:09:37.060
- Aqualad and Donna Troy.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.570
Another sidekick, Jason Todd, is off the grid.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:42.860
Wonder Woman must be well aware that the same
Deathstroke the Titans struggled with this

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:47.440
season is the one who murdered her Themysciran
sisters for money years earlier.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:51.370
And then there's Superman, who by now must
know that a young man who is a merging of

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:57.149
his DNA and Lex Luthor's exists and has gone
on a number of rampages in San Francisco.

00:09:57.149 --> 00:09:58.149
So where are they?

00:09:58.149 --> 00:10:02.380
At the very least how could Wonder Woman,
Aquaman, and Superman not get more involved

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.860
in the lives of the Titans?

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.790
Maybe Bruce Wayne acts as a buffer between
the League and the Titans, and off-screen

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.700
he might be urging his fellow Leaguers to
not interfere.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:14.790
But particularly with what we know of Wonder
Woman's warrior sense of honor, the notion

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:19.360
she would allow so many fellow Themyscirans
to fall without getting involved more directly

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:20.560
seems strange.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.800
Eh, you know what?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.990
Maybe Dick just told them all to stay away.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:27.209
You know how he can be.

00:10:27.209 --> 00:10:32.560
"F--- Batman."

